{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"19730d97-f87f-4246-8fb6-701056ec2a03","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \\\"sharpened, not soothed.\\\"\\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads\\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE, 5/5. →Tier A prioritization-slate\\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\\n- **Personal site (10/2)**: scroll-craft stays LOCAL; Artifact is live site. →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\\n- **SW/Tech Review (10/1)**: Erin asked; NEXT Teams 10/2, ET by 11/30. →`SoftwareTech_Review/docs/`\\n- **Machine split (9/24)**: Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD. →handoff 2026-09-24-machine-split\\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\\n- **Sleep sched (9/16)**: R1 merged; NEXT night/early-kickoff. →`sleep-scheduler/`\\n- **TypeSafe (10/2)**: MAINTENANCE (Eric's call). Router, Zotero classify, verifier kept; no new Jev hunting. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\\n- **Flint (9/29)**: Waves 1+2 queued. NEXT Eric: OneDrive keep/drop, 2 verify. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **42Analytics (10/2)**: 152 entries PROMOTED to vault. NEXT captions (429s) on Mac. →`42Analytics/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **VB GRID (10/2)**: fix in Box; await Mike, then merge. →`Volleyball_GRID/docs/`\\n- **PFF DB (9/22)**: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Win: `Desktop\\\\DEV` syncs via Drive (robocopy retired 9/22). No large DBs/junctions: renv via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, PFF via `PFF_DB`.\\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- None open. (OKR gate + OKRs_2026-27 CLOSED 10/2: Eric not developing further.)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\\n\\n- **perch-pull** ×1 (2026-10-01 11:55 → 2026-10-01 11:55 UTC): error exit=1 after 3 attempt(s) — see /Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json\\n- **daily-backup** ×1 (2026-10-02 01:37 → 2026-10-02 01:37 UTC): 2 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory, manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n- 1 unparsed line(s); see the file.\\n\\nFull log: `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Surface this once; clear the file after the user has seen it and the cause is handled.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4310 chars, updated 2026-10-02 11:26)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":758},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c5d648ac-d3e7-45e6-88ae-1248f7d3991b","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:31:04.575Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"11427f4a-8383-4d35-918e-9715ee26f83a","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
