{"parentUuid":"8e4565bf-9376-4d43-8a21-d11ef1606678","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"19730d97-f87f-4246-8fb6-701056ec2a03","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nFriday, October 02, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- Accept or flip the OneDrive keep/drop sort, then commit + push. Least-certain call: `08_ARCHIVE/PERSONAL` (69 held, 392 papers/books \\u2014 may contain training material).\\n- Verify 2 Flint sources: \\\"The System\\\" and \\\"Black Book Of Secrets\\\".\\n- Then: set the roots \\u2192 skip rules \\u2192 Jev pass on what remains.\\n- Still open from 9/28: Jev blind audit, 3 CLA primer questions, listen to the CVASPS spots.\\n- On Windows next session: in the `step1-triage` worktree, switch to `main`, pull, then delete the branch.\\n- PP_Recruiting: walk Mauro through workbook 017 (UPDATE DATA tab); first decide whether to show OG/OT as-is or trim. Then the 10 honors-benchmark decisions in `docs/2026-09-29-honors-benchmark-plan.md`.\\n- Hook failures surfaced and unresolved: `perch-pull` (exit 1), `daily-backup` (`repo-behind-blocked:global-memory`, `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics`).\\n\\n### Session (15:31)\\n\\n**Context:** Morning Mac session \\u2014 ran `/dev-sync` to pull the Windows laptop's work onto the Mac and pick a project to resume.\\n\\n**Decisions Made:**\\n- Flagged the Step 5 auto-pick (`TypeSafe_Sandbox`) as wrong and recommended **Flint** instead. TypeSafe won only on newest-commit, but that commit was a small router change; the real Windows work on 10/02 was the decision audit, which touched STATUS in Flint, S2, Weekly_Research_Review and RTP. Awaiting Eric's confirm.\\n- Kept both sides of two clashing daily-log files in `global-memory` rather than choosing one \\u2014 logs, not settings.\\n\\n**Lessons Learned:**\\n- Newest-commit-wins failed *again* as a project picker (same lesson as the 10/01 session with graphify-out / CommandCentre). The dev-sync Step 5 rule needs a better signal than recency \\u2014 the repos touched by the most recent *session's* STATUS edits are the real candidates.\\n- The memory repo being behind was the cause of the `daily-backup` failure (`repo-behind-blocked:global-memory`). This sync pulled it, so the next nightly run should pass.\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- Eric to pick: TypeSafe_Sandbox or Flint (recommendation: Flint).\\n- `perch-pull` still failing (exit 1) \\u2014 log at `~/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json`. Not fixed.\\n- `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics` in daily-backup still open.\\n- TypeSafe (if chosen): verify the Mac API key, run `smoke_test.py` on the Mac, copy permission-gate hook files to `~/.claude/permission-gate/`.\\n\\n**Sync result (for the record):** DEV root `~/DEV`; 147 repos checked; 16 pulled; `SoftwareTech_Review` cloned; uncommitted work saved in `graphify-out` and `KeystoneOS`; memory repo took 10 commits from Windows (newest \\\"Closeout 2026-10-02: decision audit session state\\\"); memory mirror paired 15 projects, 3 files replaced by newer Windows versions; 27 active / 118 dormant repos; no `.from-*` files; ended clean.\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":764},"type":"attachment","uuid":"afd2a05f-e279-420e-86c5-dea2681e2fa3","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:31:04.577Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"11427f4a-8383-4d35-918e-9715ee26f83a","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"afd2a05f-e279-420e-86c5-dea2681e2fa3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"19730d97-f87f-4246-8fb6-701056ec2a03","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n  <ctx_commands>\\n    \\\"ctx stats\\\" | \\\"ctx-stats\\\" | \\\"/ctx-stats\\\" | context savings question\\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx doctor\\\" | \\\"ctx-doctor\\\" | \\\"/ctx-doctor\\\" | diagnose context-mode\\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx upgrade\\\" | \\\"ctx-upgrade\\\" | \\\"/ctx-upgrade\\\" | update context-mode\\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx purge\\\" | \\\"ctx-purge\\\" | \\\"/ctx-purge\\\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\\n\\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \\\"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\\\"\\n  </ctx_commands>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":766},"type":"attachment","uuid":"363adf98-a2d9-4b77-b1c8-beb693b7c250","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:31:04.581Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"11427f4a-8383-4d35-918e-9715ee26f83a","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"363adf98-a2d9-4b77-b1c8-beb693b7c250","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \"sharpened, not soothed.\"\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n---\n\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE, 5/5. →Tier A prioritization-slate\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\n- **Personal site (10/2)**: scroll-craft stays LOCAL; Artifact is live site. →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\n- **SW/Tech Review (10/1)**: Erin asked; NEXT Teams 10/2, ET by 11/30. →`SoftwareTech_Review/docs/`\n- **Machine split (9/24)**: Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD. →handoff 2026-09-24-machine-split\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\n- **Sleep sched (9/16)**: R1 merged; NEXT night/early-kickoff. →`sleep-scheduler/`\n- **TypeSafe (10/2)**: MAINTENANCE (Eric's call). Router, Zotero classify, verifier kept; no new Jev hunting. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\n- **Flint (9/29)**: Waves 1+2 queued. NEXT Eric: OneDrive keep/drop, 2 verify. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **42Analytics (10/2)**: 152 entries PROMOTED to vault. NEXT captions (429s) on Mac. →`42Analytics/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **VB GRID (10/2)**: fix in Box; await Mike, then merge. →`Volleyball_GRID/docs/`\n- **PFF DB (9/22)**: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`\n\n## Environment Notes\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n- Win: `Desktop\\DEV` syncs via Drive (robocopy retired 9/22). No large DBs/junctions: renv via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, PFF via `PFF_DB`.\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\n\n## Pending Decisions\n- None open. (OKR gate + OKRs_2026-27 CLOSED 10/2: Eric not developing further.)\n\n---\n\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\n\n- **perch-pull** ×1 (2026-10-01 11:55 → 2026-10-01 11:55 UTC): error exit=1 after 3 attempt(s) — see /Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json\n- **daily-backup** ×1 (2026-10-02 01:37 → 2026-10-02 01:37 UTC): 2 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory, manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\n- 1 unparsed line(s); see the file.\n\nFull log: `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Surface this once; clear the file after the user has seen it and the cause is handled.\n\n---\n\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\n\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4310 chars, updated 2026-10-02 11:26)","## Today\nFriday, October 02, 2026\n\n---\n\n## Knowledge Base\n\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here — read it only when a question actually needs it:\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`\n\n---\n\n## Recent Daily Log\n\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Accept or flip the OneDrive keep/drop sort, then commit + push. Least-certain call: `08_ARCHIVE/PERSONAL` (69 held, 392 papers/books — may contain training material).\n- Verify 2 Flint sources: \"The System\" and \"Black Book Of Secrets\".\n- Then: set the roots → skip rules → Jev pass on what remains.\n- Still open from 9/28: Jev blind audit, 3 CLA primer questions, listen to the CVASPS spots.\n- On Windows next session: in the `step1-triage` worktree, switch to `main`, pull, then delete the branch.\n- PP_Recruiting: walk Mauro through workbook 017 (UPDATE DATA tab); first decide whether to show OG/OT as-is or trim. Then the 10 honors-benchmark decisions in `docs/2026-09-29-honors-benchmark-plan.md`.\n- Hook failures surfaced and unresolved: `perch-pull` (exit 1), `daily-backup` (`repo-behind-blocked:global-memory`, `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics`).\n\n### Session (15:31)\n\n**Context:** Morning Mac session — ran `/dev-sync` to pull the Windows laptop's work onto the Mac and pick a project to resume.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Flagged the Step 5 auto-pick (`TypeSafe_Sandbox`) as wrong and recommended **Flint** instead. TypeSafe won only on newest-commit, but that commit was a small router change; the real Windows work on 10/02 was the decision audit, which touched STATUS in Flint, S2, Weekly_Research_Review and RTP. Awaiting Eric's confirm.\n- Kept both sides of two clashing daily-log files in `global-memory` rather than choosing one — logs, not settings.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- Newest-commit-wins failed *again* as a project picker (same lesson as the 10/01 session with graphify-out / CommandCentre). The dev-sync Step 5 rule needs a better signal than recency — the repos touched by the most recent *session's* STATUS edits are the real candidates.\n- The memory repo being behind was the cause of the `daily-backup` failure (`repo-behind-blocked:global-memory`). This sync pulled it, so the next nightly run should pass.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Eric to pick: TypeSafe_Sandbox or Flint (recommendation: Flint).\n- `perch-pull` still failing (exit 1) — log at `~/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json`. Not fixed.\n- `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics` in daily-backup still open.\n- TypeSafe (if chosen): verify the Mac API key, run `smoke_test.py` on the Mac, copy permission-gate hook files to `~/.claude/permission-gate/`.\n\n**Sync result (for the record):** DEV root `~/DEV`; 147 repos checked; 16 pulled; `SoftwareTech_Review` cloned; uncommitted work saved in `graphify-out` and `KeystoneOS`; memory repo took 10 commits from Windows (newest \"Closeout 2026-10-02: decision audit session state\"); memory mirror paired 15 projects, 3 files replaced by newer Windows versions; 27 active / 118 dormant repos; no `.from-*` files; ended clean.\n","\n<context_window_protection>\n  <priority_instructions>\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\n  </priority_instructions>\n\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \"timeline\")\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\n       - Each command: {label: \"section header\", command: \"shell command\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\"q1\", \"q2\", ...])\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\n\n  <when_not_to_use>\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\n  </when_not_to_use>\n\n  <file_writing_policy>\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\n  </file_writing_policy>\n\n  <output_constraints>\n    <artifact_policy>\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\n    </artifact_policy>\n  </output_constraints>\n  <session_continuity>\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\n  </session_continuity>\n\n  <ctx_commands>\n    \"ctx stats\" | \"ctx-stats\" | \"/ctx-stats\" | context savings question\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\n\n    \"ctx doctor\" | \"ctx-doctor\" | \"/ctx-doctor\" | diagnose context-mode\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\n\n    \"ctx upgrade\" | \"ctx-upgrade\" | \"/ctx-upgrade\" | update context-mode\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\n\n    \"ctx purge\" | \"ctx-purge\" | \"/ctx-purge\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\n\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\"\n  </ctx_commands>\n\n</context_window_protection>"],"hookName":"SessionStart","toolUseID":"SessionStart","hookEvent":"SessionStart"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a9271cf3-9fb7-469f-85af-5a41d3ed5bdc","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:31:04.582Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nSessionStart hook additional context: ## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \"sharpened, not soothed.\"\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n---\n\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE, 5/5. →Tier A prioritization-slate\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\n- **Personal site (10/2)**: scroll-craft stays LOCAL; Artifact is live site. →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\n- **SW/Tech Review (10/1)**: Erin asked; NEXT Teams 10/2, ET by 11/30. →`SoftwareTech_Review/docs/`\n- **Machine split (9/24)**: Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD. →handoff 2026-09-24-machine-split\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\n- **Sleep sched (9/16)**: R1 merged; NEXT night/early-kickoff. →`sleep-scheduler/`\n- **TypeSafe (10/2)**: MAINTENANCE (Eric's call). Router, Zotero classify, verifier kept; no new Jev hunting. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\n- **Flint (9/29)**: Waves 1+2 queued. NEXT Eric: OneDrive keep/drop, 2 verify. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **42Analytics (10/2)**: 152 entries PROMOTED to vault. NEXT captions (429s) on Mac. →`42Analytics/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **VB GRID (10/2)**: fix in Box; await Mike, then merge. →`Volleyball_GRID/docs/`\n- **PFF DB (9/22)**: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`\n\n## Environment Notes\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n- Win: `Desktop\\DEV` syncs via Drive (robocopy retired 9/22). No large DBs/junctions: renv via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, PFF via `PFF_DB`.\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\n\n## Pending Decisions\n- None open. (OKR gate + OKRs_2026-27 CLOSED 10/2: Eric not developing further.)\n\n---\n\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\n\n- **perch-pull** ×1 (2026-10-01 11:55 → 2026-10-01 11:55 UTC): error exit=1 after 3 attempt(s) — see /Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json\n- **daily-backup** ×1 (2026-10-02 01:37 → 2026-10-02 01:37 UTC): 2 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory, manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\n- 1 unparsed line(s); see the file.\n\nFull log: `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Surface this once; clear the file after the user has seen it and the cause is handled.\n\n---\n\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\n\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4310 chars, updated 2026-10-02 11:26)\n## Today\nFriday, October 02, 2026\n\n---\n\n## Knowledge Base\n\n319 compiled articles (237 con